103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534990 true] [17592186325238 1111 #uuid "adb6bb8a-beba-534c-a6e7-03dce1a7ddbb" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325239 1034 "II, III, and IV only" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325239 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534990 true] [17592186325239 1111 #uuid "43aee250-21fe-5003-930d-7b7f3dfe8d25" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325240 1017 #edb/ref 17592186325241 13194139534990 true] [17592186325240 1089 "q-105669" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325240 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534990 true] [17592186325240 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/assets/2414de6e2129d4fceaae304d16f9be0c91a545e5a8544b2033f353ddb2e581b9.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$\n- $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$\n- $\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction.\n- $F$ is irrotational" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325240 1113 #uuid "6abbf08a-0012-57db-b3d3-a7f6df148551" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325240 1145 "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/assets/86aee33cdfa96ac0a61468cc9657e791e399f31c024cdbc3a932193dc897d534.png)\n\nIf $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement II is true, whereas statement I is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would rotate counterclockwise. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Using our right hand, if we wrap our fingers in the direction of rotation (counterclockwise), our thumb will point away from the screen. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F$ also points away from the screen, in the direction of increasing $z.$\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not irrotational.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325241 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325242 13194139534990 true] [17592186325241 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325243 13194139534990 true] [17592186325241 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325244 13194139534990 true] [17592186325241 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325245 13194139534990 true] [17592186325241 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325246 13194139534990 true] [17592186325241 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534990 true] [17592186325241 1041 "selection" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325241 1104 #edb/ref 17592186325242 13194139534990 true] [17592186325241 1110 #uuid "efeda5be-5af7-5f86-a310-74bbf0f78d09" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325242 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325242 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534990 true] [17592186325242 1111 #uuid "4b5f5b69-11f2-5abe-857c-0113af148026" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325243 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325243 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534990 true] [17592186325243 1111 #uuid "cf04c716-49b9-5125-9c34-3accb77c41db" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325244 1034 "I, III, and IV only" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325244 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534990 true] [17592186325244 1111 #uuid "cd5f0ae5-7ab1-551b-a7a7-ed0f22f09dd4" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325245 1034 "III only" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325245 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534990 true] [17592186325245 1111 #uuid "a7f822a6-31f9-5355-9ab9-f4a3f5d1f5d3" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325246 1034 "II only" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325246 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534990 true] [17592186325246 1111 #uuid "30b561a9-e388-5481-b8e2-1964f17def2b" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325247 1017 #edb/ref 17592186325248 13194139534990 true] [17592186325247 1089 "q-105671" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325247 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534990 true] [17592186325247 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/assets/4c38294780ac6d5079b759f39a7dbd4944b1c3c21495245dfd314ec180c0434e.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$\n- $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$\n- $F$ is irrotational\n- $\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction." 13194139534990 true] [17592186325247 1113 #uuid "458941dc-3c54-5698-ae7a-8a9f06bcbbb2" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325247 1145 "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/assets/979b63f21e56924bd7880f9487cf829089e38cf14d287e70196c7a661e41f97f.png)\n\nMoreover, if $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, whereas statement II is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would not rotate. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ the vector field $F$ is irrotational.\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ it points in neither the positive nor the negative $z$-direction.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325248 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325249 13194139534990 true] [17592186325248 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325250 13194139534990 true] [17592186325248 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325251 13194139534990 true] [17592186325248 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325252 13194139534990 true] [17592186325248 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325253 13194139534990 true] [17592186325248 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534990 true] [17592186325248 1041 "selection" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325248 1104 #edb/ref 17592186325250 13194139534990 true] [17592186325248 1110 #uuid "4f9e8950-1c18-5589-b47d-21fa961d80f2" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325249 1034 "I and IV only" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325249 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534990 true] [17592186325249 1111 #uuid "14063c97-e555-57e2-9e58-fa29058332d5" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325250 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325250 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534990 true] [17592186325250 1111 #uuid "cbcf174a-5c19-539b-96e8-961e5f63c395" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325251 1034 "II and IV only" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325251 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534990 true] [17592186325251 1111 #uuid "279d3db1-6221-5d41-9e6d-52537ba17f77" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325252 1034 "I, III, and IV only" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325252 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534990 true] [17592186325252 1111 #uuid "02d82b73-2c81-5c2c-a7ff-bf7b958d8bef" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325253 1034 "II only" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325253 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534990 true] [17592186325253 1111 #uuid "45617ea1-a22b-5fb8-9452-abe439dfb666" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325254 1017 #edb/ref 17592186325255 13194139534990 true] [17592186325254 1089 "q-105672" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325254 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534990 true] [17592186325254 1100 "Consider the vector field $F={e}^{y+z}\\,i+j+xyz\\,k.$ Evaluate $∇\\times F$ at the point  $(2,1,-1).$" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325254 1113 #uuid "155bec12-a4b6-5c96-ba0a-161752e85f84" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325254 1145 "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ {e}^{y+z} & 1 & xyz\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xyz)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(1)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xyz)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{y+z})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{y+z})]k \\\\  & =(xz-0)i-(yz-{e}^{y+z})j+(0-{e}^{y+z})k \\\\  & =xz\\,i+({e}^{y+z}-yz)j-{e}^{y+z}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{curl}\\,F$ at the point $(2,1,-1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\text{curl}\\,F)(2,1,-1) & =2(-1)\\,i+({e}^{1+(-1)}-1(-1))j-{e}^{1+(-1)}\\,k \\\\  & =-2\\,i+2\\,j-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325255 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325256 13194139534990 true] [17592186325255 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325257 13194139534990 true] [17592186325255 1000 #edb/ref 17592186