0 true] [17592186325268 1145 "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y) & y{z}^{2} & (x-z)\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x-z)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(y{z}^{2})]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x-z)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y))]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y{z}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y))]k \\\\  & =(0-2yz)i-(1-0)j+(0-\\frac{1}{x+y})k \\\\  & =-2yz\\,i-j-\\frac{1}{x+y}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{curl}\\,F$ at the point $(2,-1,3),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\text{curl}\\,F)(2,-1,3) & =-2(-1)(3)\\,i-j-\\frac{1}{2+(-1)}\\,k \\\\  & =6\\,i-j-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325269 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325270 13194139534990 true] [17592186325269 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325271 13194139534990 true] [17592186325269 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325272 13194139534990 true] [17592186325269 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325273 13194139534990 true] [17592186325269 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325274 13194139534990 true] [17592186325269 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534990 true] [17592186325269 1041 "selection" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325269 1104 #edb/ref 17592186325273 13194139534990 true] [17592186325269 1110 #uuid "01651cd2-1bd5-5617-b374-127c3977f291" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325270 1034 "i+2\\,j+3\\,k" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325270 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534990 true] [17592186325270 1111 #uuid "84405628-33f9-5791-a299-783052ed3a37" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325271 1034 "-3\\,j+2\\,k" 13194139534990 true] [17592186325271 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534990 true]